The central family splits in two ways, and both are problematic under the stated gates: finding one De Bruijn Hamiltonian cycle is linear-time via an Euler tour, while finding the full \(q-1\) arc-disjoint collection is only conjectured in this paper and supported by a few fixed examples. I’m now checking the repository’s rejection format and quantifying the “mechanical cost versus compact route” at the largest answer size allowed by G9, so the decision is reviewable rather than abstract-only.
